  "details": "- CVE-2026-6471: logical decoding: require the output plugin to be a\n  recognised, installed plugin rather than an arbitrary path, so a\n  non-superuser holding REPLICATION can no longer make the server dlopen any\n  file it can read (CVSS 7.2)\n- CVE-2026-16239: portal/cursor lifecycle: re-creating a cursor with different\n  result types no longer leaves the old tuple descriptor in place, closing the\n  type confusion that followed (CVSS 8.8)\n- CVE-2026-18408: pg_dump: quote the \\restrict meta-command argument so a\n  malicious superuser on the origin server cannot inject psql input that runs\n  at restore time (CVSS 8.8); completes the CVE-2025-8714 fix",
